    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=How many employees does '{{ $('Get Vendor Record').first().json.company_name }}' ({{ $('Get Vendor Record').first().json.website }}) have?\n\nKnown LinkedIn URL: {{ $('Get Vendor Record').first().json.linkedin_url || 'none' }}\n\nUse the search tool. Try these queries:\n1. \"{{ $('Get Vendor Record').first().json.company_name }}\" employees site:linkedin.com/company\n2. \"{{ $('Get Vendor Record').first().json.company_name }}\" number of employees\n\nFrom the search results, find the employee count. Prefer LinkedIn's \"employees on LinkedIn\" count if available. Also check for Crunchbase or company website mentions.\n\nReturn the employee count range using one of these exact buckets:\n- \"1-10\"\n- \"11-50\"\n- \"51-200\"\n- \"201-1000\"\n- \"1001-5000\"\n- \"5000+\"\n\nIf you find an exact number, also return it. If you cannot determine the employee count with medium or higher confidence, return your best guess with confidence=\"low\".\n\nLimit the use of the search tool to twice (2 times).",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {}
      },
